    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d208">

                <pb facs="0421" n="403" xml:id="pg403"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.AA/7–146: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-07-01T19:00:00-04:00">July 1, 1946—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5121. Herschel Johnson has been having conversations in New York with Cadogan on
                    question of membership in United Nations. Urgency is great because of July 15
                    date in Resolution on Membership passed by Security Council. Cadogan referred
                    certain questions raised by Johnson including position of Brit with respect to
                    Italy, Austria, ex-satellites, and Albania, and question whether inquiry should
                    be made as to intention of Irish, to London some days ago and has not had
                    definitive instructions thereon. Please stress urgency of this matter at a high
                    level in Fonoff and urge they send Cadogan instructions on these matters
                        promptly.<anchor n="95" xml:id="d208-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d208-f1" n="95" xml:id="d208-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram 6472, July 3, 7 p.m., the Ambassador informed the Department that he
                    had seen Under Secretary Sargent in the British Foreign Office that day about
                    the membership question and that Mr. Sargent had said that the matter had been
                    urgently referred to Mr. Bevin in Paris (501.AA/7–346). Mr. Bevin, Secretary of
                    State Byrnes, and the other Foreign Ministers of the Big Five were attending a
                    meeting of the Council of Foreign Ministers.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
